# One Lantern Too Many (side quest, docs/story/side_quests.md): every festival week the children of Vallaki carry
# paper lanterns round the square for the Baron, and every week there's one lantern more than there are children. Old
# Sabin makes them, and his hands make one extra without his knowing why. Last night his grandson Sandu followed it
# out of the west gate. **Twist:** thirty years ago the Baron's first festival was a procession of boats on Lake
# Zarovich; one turned over, and the Baron wouldn't let the rest turn back, and Sabin's daughter Liliana went down
# holding her lantern up. She holds Sandu at the end of the fishers' jetty now (data/monsters/lantern_girl.json),
# waiting for someone to turn back. Reached from the town guard's news (vallaki/gate:news) and Sabin at his stall.
# Every line here is unvoiced for now.

# --- The town guard's news (vallaki/gate:news jumps here) ---

~ guard_news
quest one_lantern_too_many rumored
Town Guard: And festival nights the children carry paper lanterns round the square for the Baron. Somebody counted. Thirty-one children. Thirty-two lanterns. Every week.
Town Guard: The Baron says count again. Old Sabin makes them, at the market. Ask him; he won't know either.
-> END

# --- Old Sabin at his lantern stall (npc vallaki_sabin, the market, by day) ---

~ sabin
if quest.one_lantern_too_many == done
vallaki_sabin: Thirty-one this week. My hands made thirty-one. (He holds them up, as if they belonged to someone else.) Sandu's helping. He folds them crooked. I don't mind.
-> END
endif
if quest.one_lantern_too_many == home
-> sabin_home
endif
if flag.sabin_asked
vallaki_sabin: The lake road. Please. He's only nine.
-> END
endif
set sabin_asked
quest one_lantern_too_many asked
Narrator: An old man sits on a stool among strings of paper lanterns, folding another with fingers that know the work better than he does. He doesn't look up.
vallaki_sabin: Thirty-two. I know. Everyone tells me. I sit down to make thirty-one and my hands make thirty-two, and I don't know who it's for.
vallaki_sabin: My grandson Sandu does. He said it was the one that floats. Last night he got up and went after it, out of the west gate, in his nightshirt. The guards let him by because he was laughing.
* [Insight DC 12] (Watch his hands while he folds the extra one.) -> sabin_seen | sabin_unseen
* Where would it go? -> sabin_where

~ sabin_seen
set sabin_remembered
Narrator: He folds the thirty-second lantern differently. Smaller. A child's size. His hands slow on it, and on the last fold he stops, and looks at it.
vallaki_sabin: Liliana. Oh. Oh, no. (He puts it down very carefully.) The Baron's first festival. Boats on the lake, with lanterns, all the way out and back. Hers turned over, and he wouldn't let us turn back. All will be well, he said. We sang.
-> sabin_where

~ sabin_unseen
Narrator: An old man folding lanterns. He's very tired, and very frightened for the boy.
-> sabin_where

~ sabin_where
vallaki_sabin: Out the west gate it goes. Down to the lake. To the fishers' jetty, I'd think. Everything in Vallaki goes down to the lake in the end.
-> END

# --- The end of the fishers' jetty, at night (npc lantern_girl) ---

~ girl
if not flag.lantern_girl_met
set lantern_girl_met
cutscene sq_lantern_girl
Narrator: At the end of the jetty, over the black water, a small light bobs. It's a paper lantern, and the one holding it is a girl of about nine made of the same pale light, in a festival dress, wet through.
Narrator: She has a boy by the hand, a real one, in a nightshirt, blue with cold, standing at the very edge of the boards and smiling at nothing.
endif
lantern_girl: You came back. Nobody came back. They sang and rowed on, and I held my lantern up so they'd see me, all the way down.
lantern_girl: He came. He saw the lantern. He's going to come in with me so I won't be by myself any more.
* Let him go. He's cold. -> girl_plead
* [if flag.sabin_remembered and not flag.lantern_girl_heard] Liliana. Your father remembers. -> girl_father
* [Athletics DC 13] (Take Bluto's old boat out to where she went down, and dive for her lantern.) -> girl_lantern | girl_lantern_lost
* (Draw your weapons.) -> fight

~ girl_plead
lantern_girl: He isn't cold. He's with me. You're going to row away. Everybody rows away.
-> fight

~ girl_father
set lantern_girl_heard
lantern_girl: Papa? (The light of her flickers.) He makes the lanterns. He made me one every week. I counted.
lantern_girl: He didn't turn back either.
* [Athletics DC 13] (Then we will. Take the boat out to where she went down, and dive for her lantern.) -> girl_lantern | girl_lantern_lost
* (Draw your weapons.) -> fight

~ girl_lantern
set lantern_girl_rested
quest one_lantern_too_many home
Narrator: The water out there is black and so cold it stops your breath. On the bottom, in the weed, a little tin lantern frame, the paper long gone, still holding the stub of a candle.
Narrator: You bring it up. In the boat, it lights by itself. On the jetty, the girl lets go of the boy's hand to hold her hands out for it.
lantern_girl: Somebody turned back.
Narrator: She takes the light from you, and she goes out with it, like a candle at a window when someone finally comes home. Sandu sits down on the boards and starts to cry, which is the first sensible thing he's done all night.
approve liriel_dawnsong +3 godrick_pendlebrook +2 thistle +2 wren_featherfoot +2 ratatoille +1: You turned back for a drowned girl's lantern
-> END

~ girl_lantern_lost
Narrator: The cold drives you back up before you reach the bottom, gasping. Up on the jetty the girl watches you climb back into the boat, and her light goes hard and white.
lantern_girl: You're rowing away.
-> fight

~ fight
combat lantern_girl

# --- Bringing Sandu home (the jetty after the fight, npc vallaki_sandu) ---

~ sandu
if quest.one_lantern_too_many == home or quest.one_lantern_too_many == done
vallaki_sandu: I fold them crooked. Grandpa says that's how you can tell they're mine.
-> END
endif
quest one_lantern_too_many home
vallaki_sandu: (His teeth are going like a sewing machine.) She was nice. She just didn't want to be on her own. Can we go home? I'm very cold.
-> END

# --- Sabin, when Sandu's home (sabin jumps here) ---

~ sabin_home
quest one_lantern_too_many done
Narrator: Sabin doesn't say anything at first. He holds the boy and rocks him on the stool, among the strings of paper lanterns, the way you'd rock a much smaller child.
if flag.lantern_girl_rested and not flag.lantern_girl_slain
vallaki_sabin: You turned back for her. Somebody turned back. (He takes a little woven ring of willow and thread from a hook over the stall.) She made this the week before. For catching the bad dreams, she said. It caught some. Take it.
else
vallaki_sabin: She's gone, then. Thirty years in the cold, and gone. (He takes a little woven ring of willow and thread from a hook over the stall.) She made this the week before. For catching the bad dreams, she said. Take it. I've had enough dreams.
endif
give dream_weaver
gold +40
approve godrick_pendlebrook +1 liriel_dawnsong +1 wren_featherfoot +2: You brought Sabin's grandson home from the lake
-> END
